---topic---
path: root
title: Motorcycle Dashboard Manual
body:
Welcome to the motorcycle dashboard manual.
Use the menu to open a topic, then tap Back or Home to navigate.
---end---

---topic---
path: root/getting-started
title: Getting Started
body:
Power on the dashboard and wait for the boot sequence to complete.
Tap a topic to learn more about each subsystem.
---end---

---topic---
path: root/getting-started/display-overview
title: Display Overview
body:
The home screen shows speed, RPM, throttle, ABS status, engine temperature, and battery voltage.
Swipe left or press the Manual button to return to the main dashboard.
---end---

---topic---
path: root/getting-started/manual-navigation
title: Manual Navigation
body:
Tap a topic tile to open it.
Use the Back button to return to the previous topic or Home to return to the manual menu.
---end---

---topic---
path: root/safety
title: Riding Safety
body:
Always wear protective gear and obey traffic regulations.
Use Rain or Track modes only when conditions are appropriate.
---end---

---topic---
path: root/safety/traction-control
title: Traction Control
body:
Traction control limits wheel spin when sensors detect slip.
Use the Back button to return to Safety topics.
---end---

---topic---
path: root/safety/abs
title: Anti-lock Braking
body:
ABS prevents wheel lock during hard braking.
The dashboard alert flashes if the system detects a fault.
---end---

---topic---
path: root/maintenance
title: Maintenance
body:
Follow the service interval schedule to extend component lifespan.
Log maintenance events using the `Maintenance` topic entries.
---end---

---topic---
path: root/maintenance/oil
title: Engine Oil
body:
Check engine oil every 1,000 km.
Replace with the manufacturer-approved grade.
---end---

---topic---
path: root/maintenance/battery
title: Battery Care
body:
Inspect battery terminals monthly.
Recharge the battery if voltage drops below 12.1 V.
---end---
